md.append("\n# Deliverable C — Research-integrity audit\n")
md.append(f"""**Datasets actually used:** HAM10000 (10,015 images, 7,470 lesions; Harvard Dataverse copy in `data/HAM10000`); HAM10000 expert lesion segmentations (`HAM10000_segmentations_lesion_tschandl.zip`, downloaded from Harvard Dataverse during this revision, 10,015 masks); PAD-UFES-20 (2,298 images; 2,106 after mapping). ISIC 2018 Task 1 was **not** used (the original manuscript's attribution of the masks to it was inaccurate).

**Experiments actually executed:** full re-training of DenseNet121 for seeds 42, 43, 44, 45, 46 (60-epoch one-cycle, batch 32, AdamW, AMP) plus one 100-epoch sensitivity run (seed 42); per-seed temperature scaling; test and PAD inference; Grad-CAM++ (predicted class, all 990 test images; true-class maps also computed); LSAS and null/ceiling baselines; deletion/insertion faithfulness (mean-image baseline: all seeds; blurred baseline: seed 42 only); MC-dropout stability (300 images, 15 passes); ITA (all 10,015 images); PAD decomposition (all seeds); domain-gap and adaptation ladder (all seeds).

**Final checkpoints / epochs (selection rule: best val_sel macro-F1):** {', '.join(f"seed {r.run[4:]}: epoch {int(r.best_epoch)}" for _, r in cv[cv.run.str.match('^seed4[2-6]$')].iterrows())}. Test set was never used for selection.

**Final sample sizes:** train 8,020; val_sel 502; val_cal 503; test 990 (747 lesions); correct/misclassified in seed 42: 810/180; ITA strata (test, v1, all images) 808/150/32; PAD 2,106 (1,297 patients).

**Statistical methods:** Kruskal–Wallis (ε²), Mann–Whitney (rank-biserial), Wilcoxon signed-rank, Spearman and rank-partial correlation, Holm correction, BCa bootstrap for medians, lesion-clustered bootstrap for metrics and slopes, OLS/logistic with lesion-clustered SE, permutation test (2,000 re-pairings), Clopper–Pearson intervals, t-based CI over seeds, normal-approximation MDE.

**External datasets used:** PAD-UFES-20 only.

**Experiments added in the model-comparison revision:** ResNet50 trained under the identical protocol for seeds 42-46 (60-epoch one-cycle, same split, loss and sampler) and evaluated with the same Grad-CAM++, LSAS, faithfulness, stability and EIG/EDG code as DenseNet121; frozen-feature linear-probe baselines for both backbones (training split only; regularization chosen on val_sel); a validation-only INT8 configuration sweep (two sweeps, 28 candidate configurations, seed-42 models, 502 val_sel images); post-training INT8 quantization of all ten FP32 checkpoints with the validation-selected configuration, a group-wise mixed-precision sensitivity analysis and a quantization-aware pilot for the seed-42 models (training split only, best epoch on val_sel; the pilot did not improve on post-training quantization and was not extended), and the DenseNet121 alternative with dense block 1 in FP32; INT8 evaluation on the 990 test images and PAD-UFES-20; efficiency benchmark (parameters, serialized size, CPU and GPU latency) on an otherwise idle machine; uniform per-seed metric computation from saved logits (validated by reproducing the DenseNet121 headline numbers of Section 4.1 exactly); paired and unpaired statistical comparisons; donor-count, baseline and donor-selection sensitivity of EIG/EDG (Section 4.11); and a calibration-sensitivity check (all confidence-related conclusions recomputed from uncalibrated probabilities). Not done: explanation maps from quantized networks (gradients are undefined through integer kernels), other architectures, other explanation methods or layers, and any reader study.

**Analyses that could not be performed / were limited:** (i) independent darker-skin dermoscopic validation with masks — no such data in the supplied materials; public diverse datasets are clinical photographs without lesion masks (assessed from the literature, not downloaded); (ii) blurred-baseline faithfulness only for seed 42 (computational cost); (iii) original epoch-37 checkpoint and original Kaggle outputs were not in the folder, so the legacy model could not be re-evaluated — only its logged training history was used; (iv) PAD images >1,024 px were downscaled before hair removal (deviation quantified: prediction change {100 * (1 - RX.DG[42]['hair_removal_deviation']['agree_all']):.0f}% of images vs. resize-only); (v) patient-level disjointness of HAM10000 cannot be verified (no patient IDs); (vi) held-out tone-calibration analysis of the original was not repeated (not informative about fairness); (vii) the repository's `src/` domain-shift pipeline (ConvNeXt/5-class) belongs to a different study and was not used.

**Deviations from the original pipeline (disclosed in the manuscript):** full annealed schedule; val_sel/val_cal split for selection vs. calibration; official Dataverse masks; all-images explanation analysis; single GPU (RTX 4050) with mixed precision; DataLoader augmentation performed on cached 224×224 hair-removed images (identical to the original Resize-first order).

**Remaining limitations:** see manuscript §6. Notably, seed 42 (the reference seed for detailed tables) is the best seed on accuracy/macro-F1; temperature scaling did not improve test ECE; skin-tone results are seed-sensitive.

**Reference verification:** 44 of the 62 references were matched to Crossref or arXiv records (title, authors, year, venue, DOI). The remaining items are conference proceedings or older papers without a DOI lookup (Guo 2017, Gal 2016, Ovadia 2019, Adebayo 2018, Hooker 2019, Yeh 2019, Lipton 2018 [cited only in Methods], Bouthillier 2021, Holm 1979, Brier 1950); their authors, titles, venues and years are well established but volume/page details were not machine-checked and should be spot-checked before submission. Page ranges I could not confirm were omitted.

**Fabrication check:** every number in the manuscript is generated by `build_manuscript.py` from files in `out/results/` produced by the scripts in `revision/`; no value was typed in by hand except the legacy epoch-37 values quoted from the original run's log (best val F1 0.6916, LR ≈2e-4, train acc 0.949) and the original manuscript's headline numbers cited for comparison.
""")
